/-!
# G.2.5 counting and its binary series application

The order formula is proved from the earlier marked equivariant layer
identifications, unipotent-radical coordinates and literal star-kernel
comparison. The binary application additionally uses the actual homogeneous
cubic action from 12.8.5(1), proving S₂=V, r=0 and S₃=S.

The normal-series refinement and residual restriction calculations are
available. For n>1 they expose a source obstruction: every complete chief
series of the actual two-residual L₁ has a noncentral two-factor of order
2^n, which cannot be a natural plane of order 2^(2n). The all-natural part
of the requested chief description would therefore force n=1. This does
not prove that the source setup forces n=1 or construct a larger-field
counterexample to all its hypotheses. The general source statement still
requires resolution; the binary chief-count assembly also remains open.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, combined manuscript (1 March 2004),
G.2.5(8) and 12.8.8(4–5), printed pp.335–336,851–852.
-/
